 edge cases\");\n231:   assert(Array.isArray(guide1.hints) && guide1.hints.length >= 3, \"Guide provides 3 progressive hints\");\n232: \n233:   // [5] Test Section B: Learn the Pattern\n234:   console.log(\"\\n[5] Testing Section B: Learn the Pattern (DSA Teaching Content):\");\n235:   assert(wsHtml.includes('Learn the Pattern'), \"Section B tab header present\");\n236:   assert(wsHtml.includes('Why This Pattern Is Useful'), \"Explains why pattern is useful\");\n237:   assert(wsHtml.includes('Prerequisite Concepts'), \"Prerequisites explained\");\n238:   assert(wsHtml.includes('Small Walkthrough Example'), \"Illustrative walkthrough example present\");\n239:   assert(wsHtml.includes('How To Approach The Solution (Step-by-Step)'), \"Intended 3-step approach present\");\n240:   assert(guide1.whyUseful.includes('O('), \"Why useful explains algorithmic complexity O(...)\");\n241:   assert(guide1.intendedApproach.length === 3, \"Intended approach has 3 clear actionable steps\");\n242: \n243:   // [6] Test Section C: Try It Yourself (Code Editor, Hints, Solution Reveal & Cache)\n244:   console.log(\"\\n[6] Testing Section C: Try It Yourself (Editor, Hints, Solution, Auto-Save):\");\n245:   assert(wsHtml.includes('workspaceCodeEditor'), \"Code editor textarea present\");\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
